---
function arrow(x1: number, y1: number, x2: number, y2: number) {
  const a = Math.atan2(y2 - y1, x2 - x1);
  const p1 = [x2 - 8 * Math.cos(a - 0.45), y2 - 8 * Math.sin(a - 0.45)];
  const p2 = [x2 - 8 * Math.cos(a + 0.45), y2 - 8 * Math.sin(a + 0.45)];
  return {
    line: `M ${x1} ${y1} L ${x2 - 6 * Math.cos(a)} ${y2 - 6 * Math.sin(a)}`,
    head: `${x2},${y2} ${p1[0].toFixed(1)},${p1[1].toFixed(1)} ${p2[0].toFixed(1)},${p2[1].toFixed(1)}`,
  };
}
---
<figure class="gp">
  <div class="gp-scroll">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 900 230" role="img" aria-label="Three events cancel the request context: the client connection closes, the request is canceled, or ServeHTTP returns. Any goroutine started with that context is then told to stop.">
    {[
      { y: 24, en: "The client's connection closes", vi: 'Kết nối của client đóng', bad: false },
      { y: 92, en: 'The request is canceled (HTTP/2)', vi: 'Request bị hủy (HTTP/2)', bad: false },
      { y: 160, en: 'ServeHTTP returns', vi: 'ServeHTTP return', bad: true },
    ].map((c) => {
      const a = arrow(320, c.y + 22, 410, 115);
      return (
        <g>
          <rect x="20" y={c.y} width="300" height="44" rx="8" class={c.bad ? 'box bad' : 'box'} />
          <text x="170" y={c.y + 27} text-anchor="middle" class={c.bad ? 'red' : 'strong'}>
            <tspan data-lang-en>{c.en}</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>{c.vi}</tspan>
          </text>
          <g class={c.bad ? 'arrow bad' : 'arrow'}><path d={a.line} /><polygon points={a.head} /></g>
        </g>
      );
    })}
    <rect x="410" y="80" width="200" height="70" rx="8" class="box" />
    <text x="510" y="109" text-anchor="middle" class="strong"><tspan data-lang-en>The request's context</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>Context của request</tspan></text>
    <text x="510" y="130" text-anchor="middle" class="strong"><tspan data-lang-en>is canceled</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>bị hủy</tspan></text>
    {(() => { const a = arrow(610, 115, 690, 115); return <g class="arrow"><path d={a.line} /><polygon points={a.head} /></g>; })()}
    <rect x="690" y="80" width="190" height="70" rx="8" class="box" />
    <text x="785" y="109" text-anchor="middle" class="strong"><tspan data-lang-en>Goroutines using it</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>Goroutine dùng nó</tspan></text>
    <text x="785" y="130" text-anchor="middle" class="strong"><tspan data-lang-en>are told to stop</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>được báo dừng</tspan></text>
  </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span data-lang-en>Any one of these three events cancels the request's context. The last one is the surprise: the handler finishing is enough, even when background work was meant to continue.</span>
    <span data-lang-vi>Chỉ cần một trong ba sự kiện này là context của request bị hủy. Cái cuối là cái gây bất ngờ: handler chạy xong là đủ, kể cả khi việc chạy nền định làm tiếp.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .gp { margin: 2em 0; width: 100%; }
  .gp-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .gp svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 640px; height: auto; }
  .gp text { font-size: 14px; fill: var(--text-body); }
  .gp .h { font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .gp .strong { font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .gp .muted { fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .gp .red { fill: var(--red); font-weight: 700; }
  .gp .box { fill: var(--bg-alt); stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .gp .box.bad { fill: var(--red-tint-bg); stroke: var(--red); }
  .gp .bar { fill: var(--bg-alt); stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .gp .bar.bad { fill: var(--red-tint-bg); stroke: var(--red); }
  .gp .wait { fill: none; stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 1.2; stroke-dasharray: 4 3; }
  .gp .rule { stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1; }
  .gp .axis { stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .gp .dot { fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .gp .dot.bad { fill: var(--red); }
  .gp .arrow path { fill: none; stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .gp .arrow polygon { fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .gp .arrow.bad path { stroke: var(--red); }
  .gp .arrow.bad polygon { fill: var(--red); }
  .gp figcaption { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.55; text-align: center; }
</style>
